# COMPLETE PRODUCTION IMPLEMENTATION: FROM-SCRATCH TEXT-TO-IMAGE AND IMAGE-TO-IMAGE GENERATOR

## SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE SPECIFICATION

Build a complete text-to-image and image-to-image generation system using Modal.com B200:8 GPU infrastructure. The architecture combines five cutting-edge technologies published between January 7-21, 2026: Deep Delta Learning (DDL), Manifold-Constrained Hyper-Connections (mHC), Coupling Flow Matching (CFM), implemented across Zig, Futhark, Halide, Spiral, Bend programming languages. No pre-trained models, diffusion models, or existing frameworks permitted. Complete from-scratch implementation required.

## CORE ARCHITECTURAL COMPONENTS

### Component 1: Text Encoder - Deep Delta Learning Architecture

Implement complete DDL-based text encoder in Zig with following specifications:

**DDL Delta Operator Mathematical Foundation:**
- Implement Householder transformation-based rank-1 perturbation of identity matrix
- Delta Operator formula: Δ(X) = (I - β(X) · k(X)k(X)ᵀ) where β is learnable scalar gate, k is reflection direction vector
- β(X) must dynamically interpolate between: identity mapping (β=0), orthogonal projection (β=1), geometric reflection (β=2)
- Implement spectral analysis module computing complete eigensystem of Delta Operator
- Gate β acts as depth-wise step size controlling information erasure and feature writing

**Zig Implementation Requirements:**
```zig
// File: src/encoder/ddl_operator.zig
const std = @import("std");
const cuda = @import("cuda");

pub const DeltaOperator = struct {
    dimension: usize,
    beta_network: *BetaGateNetwork,
    k_network: *ReflectionVectorNetwork,
    device: cuda.Device,

    pub fn init(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, dim: usize, device: cuda.Device) !*DeltaOperator;
    pub fn computeTransform(self: *DeltaOperator, input: []f32, output: []f32) !void;
    pub fn computeSpectrum(self: *DeltaOperator, input: []f32) ![]f32;
    pub fn backward(self: *DeltaOperator, grad_output: []f32, grad_input: []f32) !void;
};

pub const BetaGateNetwork = struct {
    weights: []f32,
    bias: f32,
    pub fn forward(self: *BetaGateNetwork, features: []f32) f32;
    pub fn backward(self: *BetaGateNetwork, grad: f32) !void;
};

pub const ReflectionVectorNetwork = struct {
    weights: [][]f32,
    pub fn forward(self: *ReflectionVectorNetwork, features: []f32, output: []f32) !void;
    pub fn backward(self: *ReflectionVectorNetwork, grad: []f32) !void;
};
```

**Complete DDL Encoder Stack:**
- Tokenizer: Byte-Pair Encoding with 50,000 vocabulary
- Embedding layer: 512-dimensional vectors
- 24 DDL layers with residual connections
- Each layer: LayerNorm -> Multi-Head Attention (8 heads) -> DDL Operator -> FFN with DDL
- Output: 512-dimensional semantic latent vectors

**Memory Management:**
- Implement custom CUDA memory allocator in Zig
- GPU memory pooling with 4GB pre-allocated blocks
- Gradient checkpointing: store only layer inputs, recompute activations during backward pass

